If a clinician starts an opioid-therapy for an opioid-naive-patient then a lowest-starting-opioid-dose can often include at least 5 approximate MME-units and can often include at most 10 approximate MME-units.
If a clinician starts an opioid-therapy for an opioid-naive-patient then a lowest-starting-opioid-daily-dosage can often include at least 20 MME-units-per-day and can often include at most 30 MME-units-per-day.
